/F1 14 Tf
(4. Competitive Analysis) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
T*
() Tj
T*
(| Platform | Strength | Weakness | Missing |) Tj
T*
(|---|---|---|---|) Tj
T*
(| Collegedunia | Large SEO footprint, broad college/course/exam coverage, strong) Tj
T*
(lead-generation flows | Pages can feel cluttered, heavy content density, decision path is) Tj
T*
(not always clear | Cleaner comparison, transparent confidence, fewer distractions, faster) Tj
T*
(shortlist workflow |) Tj
T*
(| Careers360 | Strong tools ecosystem, predictors, rankings, exam coverage,) Tj
T*
(counselling-oriented flows | Tool flows can feel gated or complex, many content paths) Tj
T*
(compete for attention | Lightweight decision dashboard, simple compare-first UX, clearer) Tj
T*
(explanation of recommendation logic |) Tj
T*
(| Shiksha | Deep course and review coverage, strong college/course detail pages, useful) Tj
T*
(filters | Review trust can be hard to judge, dense pages, sponsored/lead flows may distract) Tj
T*
(| Verified review signals, cleaner metric hierarchy, stronger save-to-decision workflow |) Tj
T*
(| GetMyUni | Admission-focused content, college discovery, counselling funnel, simplified) Tj
T*
(summaries | Less structured decision tooling, content sometimes feels lead-oriented |) Tj
T*
(Stronger comparison, richer structured data, transparent fit scoring |) Tj
T*
(| Zollege | Simple college pages, SEO collections, accessible listing style | Shallower) Tj
T*
(tooling and decision support compared with larger competitors | Better backend-driven) Tj
