/F1 14 Tf
(Market Gaps) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Weak comparison UX: Most platforms provide comparison, but it is usually table-heavy and) Tj
T*
(not decision-ranked.) Tj
T*
(2. Low personalization: Discovery is mostly filter-based, not preference-based.) Tj
T*
(3. Poor decision support: Users see many facts but few clear conclusions.) Tj
T*
(4. Cluttered pages: Lead forms, ads, articles, rankings, and widgets often compete with the) Tj
T*
(student decision.) Tj
T*
(5. Missing data confidence: Platforms do not clearly show whether placement/package data is) Tj
T*
(missing, estimated, stale, or verified.) Tj
T*
(6. Shortlisting is underpowered: Saved colleges often behave like bookmarks, not a decision) Tj
T*
(workspace.) Tj
T*
(7. Performance friction: Large pages can feel slow because they combine content, ads, tools,) Tj
T*
(and widgets.) Tj
